<title>RUSSIA: Aeroflot begins Moscow-Bishkek service.</title>
<headline>Aeroflot begins Moscow-Bishkek service.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia's international carrier Aeroflot began regular passenger flights between Moscow and the Kyrgyz capital Bishkek on Monday, a company spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>&quot;We are operating an Ilyushin-62 jet that makes one flight a week on Mondays from Sheremetyevo international airport,&quot; the spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>Aeroflot and Kyrgyz national carrier Kyrgyzstan Aba Zholdoru signed a cooperation agreement last year, but it has not yet begun to function. - Viktor Anoshkin, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
</text>
